<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;ARCHIBALD ATKINSON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Archibald Atkinson was a U.S. Representative from Virginia, born in Isle of Wight County, Virginia, and received a liberal education at the College of William &amp; Mary. He served during the War of 1812 and held various positions in the Virginia legislature."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ISLE OF WIGHT COUNTY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Isle of Wight County is located in Virginia and was the birthplace of Archibald Atkinson. It is known for its historical significance and agricultural heritage."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLLEGE OF WILLIAM &amp; MARY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The College of William &amp; Mary is a private research university in Williamsburg, Virginia, where Archibald Atkinson studied law. It is one of the oldest institutions of higher learning in the United States and has a rich history dating back to 1693."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WAR OF 1812&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The War of 1812 was a military conflict fought between the United States and the British Empire, primarily over issues of trade and territorial disputes. Archibald Atkinson served during this war, contributing to the defense of the United States."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VIRGINIA HOUSE OF DELEGATES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Virginia House of Delegates is the lower house of the Virginia General Assembly, where Archibald Atkinson served from 1815 to 1817 and 1828 to 1831."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VIRGINIA SENATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Virginia Senate is the upper house of the Virginia General Assembly, where Archibald Atkinson served from 1839 to 1843."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JASON ATKINSON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Jason Atkinson is an American politician from Oregon, born in Ashland, and served as a senator in the Oregon State Senate from 2001 to 2013. He ran for the Republican nomination for Governor of Oregon in 2006 and was reelected to the Senate in 2008. He intended to run in the 2010 Oregon gubernatorial election but withdrew from the race in 2009. In 1998, Atkinson was elected to his first public office as a member of the Oregon House."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ASHLAND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ashland is a city in Southern Oregon where Jason Atkinson grew up and later represented as a senator. It is known for its cultural and educational institutions, including the Ashland Shakespeare Festival."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OREGON STATE SENATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Oregon State Senate is the upper house of the Oregon Legislative Assembly, where Jason Atkinson served from 2001 to 2013."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REPUBLICAN PARTY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Republican Party is a major political party in the United States, and Jason Atkinson is a member of this party."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2006 OREGON GUBERNATORIAL ELECTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The 2006 Oregon gubernatorial election was a political contest in which Jason Atkinson ran for the Republican nomination for Governor of Oregon."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2008 OREGON GUBERNATORIAL ELECTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The 2008 Oregon gubernatorial election was a political contest in which Jason Atkinson was reelected to the Senate."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2010 OREGON GUBERNATORIAL ELECTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The 2010 Oregon gubernatorial election was a political contest in which Jason Atkinson intended to run but withdrew from the race in 2009."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OREGON HOUSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Oregon House is the lower house of the Oregon Legislative Assembly, where Jason Atkinson was elected to his first public office in 1998."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2024 PRESIDENTIAL ELECTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The 2024 Presidential election is a future political contest involving candidates from various parties, including the Republican Party."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2024 PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"2024 Presidential candidates are individuals running for the position of President of the United States in the 2024 election."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2024 CONGRESSIONAL ELECTIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The 2024 Congressional elections involve the selection of members to serve in the U.S. House of Representatives and the U.S. Senate."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6</data>
    </node>
  </graph>
</graphml>
